hi there steve kaufman here steve  kaufman of link as you know and uh of my  blog the linguist on language  and today i want to talk about um two  things  first of all uh how important is it that  companies that have language learning  systems on the web  should be managed by people with a  formal background in language education  and second of all how do we evaluate  a learner  best and how do we evaluate whether a  program  a school or a language learning program  is affected the reason i want to talk  about this is because i have been  involved in a discussion over at kirsten  winkler's blog and i will put the  link here in the description to this  video  where someone posted saying that  people on the internet who are signing  up for these language learning programs  like live moca itake  busu  link and so forth  should be wary  because the people who run these aren't  using uh  you know experts with a proper  educational background in language  education  so that was the one point and then as i  got involved in the discussion there it  became clear that the two people on that  uh discussion uh felt very strongly that  that there had to be some kind of  objective evaluation of how effectively  people are learning  whereas i took the position that if the  learner is satisfied with his or her  progress that is really the best  uh indication now  i don't know why i get involved in these  discussions  must be because  i went skiing and came back early and my  wife went golfing  so i look at these things and i'm always  interested in  in discussions about language learning  and it came through on  linkedin where i'm a member of a group  which is called some kind of language  learning group  so i saw a reference to this discussion  and of course as usual i jumped in with  both feet  um but  to me first of all  language resources on the internet are  not schools  they are just that they are resources  uh italki is a place where you can go  and find language partners  rhino spike is a place where you can  have  any text recorded by a native speaker  link is linked as you know i believe  very much in input based language  learning and you'll find lots of  resources that will help you  access content and use audio and text  content for your language learning their  resources that's what they are  some of them are developed i would say a  lot of them actually are developed by  keen language learners  but not necessarily by people with an  educational background in  in pedagogy  does it matter of course it doesn't  matter it doesn't matter at all  and people need not be wary any more  than they're wary walking into a store  they are users  they are potential customers  they can come and look around and  in the case of link they can use it free  of charge and then decide if they want  to stay or if they want to pay for  certain additional services that cost  money or  they can download content free of charge  and take it away and do whatever they  want  so  i think it's tremendous that there are  these entrepreneurs  on the internet and also in terms of  apps  in ipod or the iphone that are creating  products for learners  and the learner can decide to buy not to  buy to stay most of them realize that on  the internet you have to offer a lot for  free in order to get people  uh to uh to use it because there's so  much stuff there it's great  it it for the first time the learner  is is treated like like a customer like  someone with some the right to choose  whereas in the average school that's not  the case  i think in most schools this the learner  is quite captive  because they have to sign up for a  semester or for a year for four years  typically they are paid for by someone  else might be in the case of immigrants  it might be the government that's  subsidizing them it might be their  parents  or someone else they might be sent there  by their employer there's so many  different situations where the learner  is just captive and so therefore the  teacher and the the person who runs the  school is free to do what they want  some of which may be very very good but  the decision very much  is with the teacher  uh so that's fine that's perhaps the by  far the largest part of the market  that's fine maybe that'll always be the  case but why would  someone not the fact that there is now  choice by the internet  that entrepreneurs such as me  i don't know if i call myself an  entrepreneur as much as  don quixote tilting at windmills but  nevertheless we put things up there  and people come and sniff and have a  look and they choose  and some do well and some don't so  to me the question of educational  background is completely irrelevant  the second issue was you know i said  it sort of challenged me well how do you  know that your learners at link are  doing well and i say because they tell  me if they're happy if they're happy  they stay if they're not happy they go  uh  and when we get testimonials from people  saying that they've never had  so much success learning languages  before that they're very happy with link  some of them say that they've  increased their score on toeic by our  many marks and that they attribute this  to link and so we get a lot of positive  feedback  very some almost our heart warming  notes of thank you from people that's  enough  um so to which the response is well  that's you know the satisfaction of the  learner is not sufficient we need an  objective evaluation well  uh of course people who want to go  to take a third party test are quite  welcome to do so and many of our  learners have done so  uh  personally if i learn language i have no  interest in having someone else evaluate  how well i'm doing in the language i  know when i understand i know when i can  communicate i know if i do better now  than i did six months ago that sense of  satisfaction achievement and progress  that i myself feel is all i need but i  recognize that for different purposes  people need some kind of a certificate  and i think that those kinds of uh  you know call it objective it's not  really objective but somewhat objective  testimony or proof of someone's level or  progress in the language they should be  done by  arms length independent testing  organizations schools should not be  handing out diplomas because that's the  other problem people go to a school in  order to get the diploma  uh so that the school controls so they  have to go through the school to get the  diploma well it shouldn't be that way i  should be able to go  and sit any exam i want in to test my  language competence and i would take it  further even in other fields  say particularly in terms of  universities and in terms of history or  literature or whatever if i can do the  test but staying with languages for now  if i can take the toeic is a good  example it's a great test  sixty dollars whatever it costs i take  the toeic it doesn't matter whether i  studied on my own whether i studied at  some institution it shouldn't matter you  know we shouldn't have a situation where  these diplomas that testify to your  language competence are issued by the  same places that are  asking you to pay money to learn there  uh in the case of link nothing prevents  people from going to a third party  to have their competence tested every  six months so that they can evaluate how  well they're doing at length but i don't  think it's up to link to do that as far  as i'm concerned it's it's almost like a  gym you know we offer facilities uh we  listen to our customers they say we want  this we want that we try to respond to  what we think is a widespread need we  want to provide a better and better  facility resource for people to use as  part of their language learning  experience and the same is true of  italki and busu and live mocha and all  these people and the learner now is put  in the position that they haven't  enjoyed before of being able to choose  so they can choose to spend time in live  mocha they can choose to spend time at  link in conjunction with perhaps going  to a school and they have much more  choice  so  i mean the conclusion to me is i think  that the the learner is the best judge  of how well they're doing i think in  most cases but many people want for a  variety of reasons personal or  professional to get a third party  evaluation go and get it from toeic or  from cambridge or from wherever  but  i don't feel that at link i'm  responsible for the results of my  learners  i'm responsible for creating the best  possible learning community environment  system we're constantly thinking up new  things that might be helpful  what the learners do with that is up to  the learners that's part and parcel of  being an independent learner is that you  go out and find the resources that suit  you  and you are responsible for your  learning  uh and we are responsible for having a  high quality uh facility now then they  come back well how do you know that your  facility is high quality unless it's  been you know vetted by again by some  board of people with  with uh you know educational credentials  well i've had enough experience with  those people to know that anything that  doesn't fit  their perception  that you know that tutors have to be  credentialed and that you have to follow  some theory that's been uh  you know as part of the the language  teaching orthodoxy and so forth that  they will simply discount what you're  doing  but i say like  can listening be bad can reading be bad  can building up your vocabulary be bad  and talking to native speakers be bad is  there anything we do at length that is  not a big part of language learning i  mean people can also learn  just by talking with people that why  does language learning have to it's not  like we're not running an engineering  school here it's all about  learning to do something that's actually  quite natural  uh  yeah so  i know i'm allowed to go to 15 so i'll  now i'll save it i'll save it for the  this other issue that i had a chat with  susannah  zareiske i hope i got it right  unfortunately our our skype conversation  was got frozen so i don't know if we're  going to put it up or not  but this whole issue of  of when should we start  speaking  and um  yeah i think i have a conversation  planned with with robert of austria on  that subject so i'll save my my views on  that  for that conversation so you may be  seeing some of these uh video exchanges  skype exchanges if we can get through  the technology at any rate uh thank you  for listening and if you're wondering  why i'm bouncing up and down is because  i'm sitting on a ball here one of these  medicine balls and it's kind of good i  like i like sitting on them also i had a  great day skiing today it was a  wonderful day here in vancouver  so thank you for listening bye for now

